n your hand with the wicked to be a malicious witness.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Numbers 14:15","note":"Now if you killed this people as one man, then the nations which have heard the fame of you will speak, saying,","source":"web"},{"ref":"Deuteronomy 2:25","note":"Today I will begin to put the dread of you and the fear of you on the peoples who are under the whole sky, who shall hear the report of you, and shall tremble…","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Kings 10:1","note":"When the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon concerning Yahweh’s name, she came to test him with hard questions.","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Chronicles 9:1","note":"When the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon, she came to test Solomon with hard questions at Jerusalem, with a very great caravan, including camels…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Job 28:22","note":"Destruction and Death say, ‘We have heard a rumor of it with our ears.’","source":"web"},{"ref":"Psalm 18:44","note":"As soon as they hear of me they shall obey me. The foreigners shall submit themselves to me.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H8089","lemma":"שֹׁ֫מַע","transliteration":"shoma","gloss":"report"},{"id":"H8090","lemma":"שְׁמַע","transliteration":"shema","gloss":"Shema"}],"senses":[{"id":"H8088B","gloss":"report","relation":"H8088B ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}